<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Paranda</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Parenda, Paranda Fort</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Paranda is a town in Dharashiv (Osmanabad) district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharashtra">Maharashtra</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, known for its large fort. The fort is traditionally attributed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahmud-gawan">Mahmud Gawan</a> in the fifteenth century and was one of the strongholds of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahmani-sultanate">Bahmani Sultanate</a>. It later passed to the Nizam Shahis of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmadnagar">Ahmadnagar</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughals</a> and the Nizams of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hyderabad">Hyderabad</a>, and keeps its moat, bastions and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/field-artillery">cannons</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/paranda.jpg" alt="Paranda" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kiranpawar3210 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mahadarwaza_of_Paranda_fort.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
